<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29171" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύσ-κολος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόλον</span>): <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of persons, prop. <i>hard to satisfy with food</i> (cf.
				<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				6.262a
			</span></i>): but, generally, <i>hard to please, discontented, fretful,
				peevish</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				942
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					1251
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ψυχὴ καὶ ἀγρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					649e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1108a30
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					791c
				</span></i>
			; of animals, <i>intractable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				174d
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			): so in Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσκόλως, ἔχειν, διακεῖσθαι πρός
			τινα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.132
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				3.33
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσκολώτερον διακεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					84e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<i>troublesome, harassing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἡ ἡνιόχησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					246b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρετοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Coac.</u>
					38
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>unpleasant</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄν τι δ. συμβῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.189
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				89
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ τι δ. πέπρακται Θηβαίοις πρὸς
					ἡμᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.176
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καιροὶ δ.</span>
			<i>difficult</i> times, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.682.33
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὑπακούειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					3.8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>difficult to explain</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>SE</u>
				180b5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1001b1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἐστι</span> it is
				<i>difficult,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Marc.
				10.24
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				1.15
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μὲν ῥάδια . . τὰ δὲ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Po.</u>
					994.24
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λως</span>
			<i>hardly, with difficulty,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Marc.
				10.23
			</span></i>,al.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
